hor\">Bright, Betty.\nDavison Art Center.\nRogan, Clare I., 1968-\nTaraba, Suzy.\nWitthus, Rutherford W., 1942-\n\nDescription\nLanguage: \tEnglish\nNotes: \t\"The covers for Counting on Chance were generated solely on press using three of the four process color printing plates (Cyan, Magenta, and Yellow) from the interior of the book, via a method used mostly for preparing the press for printing called 'make-ready.' By overprinting color, areas of image are built up on the paper by repeatedly passing the sheets through the press. The meaning of 'make-ready' is exactly as it sounds, 'to prepare.' In this sense , it is an optimistic imperative: Prepare of the experience, reader. In the true spirit of 'chance' the exact image of the cover will be generated at random when printing the book and as of this writing can only be imagined. Instructions to consistently rotate some of the sheets prior to feeding them into the press ensures variation within the edition. \" -- colophon.\nIncludes bibliographical references and index.\nPublished in conjunction with the exhibition \"Counting on chance \" held at the Davison Art Center, Wesleyan University , in Middletown, Connecticut, March 26 - May 23, 2010 -- opposite t.-p.\nOCLC Number: \t636089124\nISBN: \t\nPersistent URL: \thttp://search.lib.unc.edu/search?R=UNCb6367278\n\tView this record in the Classic Catalog\n\nTable of Contents\nForeword / by Suzy Taraba and Clare I. Rogan -- Break-through (resoluteness): work by Robin Price / essay by Betty Bright -- A conversation with Robin Price / interview by Suzy Taraba -- Catalogue raisonné / by Rutherford W. Witthus, with commentary by Robin Price -- Counting ventures: curriculum vitae.\n\nCatalog Home   |   Libraries & Collections   |   E-Research Tools   |   E-Journal Finder   |   Libraries Home\nWorldcat   |   Privacy Policy   |   Feedback  \n"}